> Original skewed3-by-3 basis

Retain rows(201,37,5),(143,25,3),(88,16,2) and delta0.75. The original report
compared before/after norms and a floating Gram determinant. Here those row-norm
observations remain, while actual native events, returned integer coordinates,
exact transform entries and computed reduction flags provide additional
evidence. On this original fixture, the completed result has an exact half
projection that the final double Gram-Schmidt observes as0.50000000000000011.
The strict computed size-reduced flag is therefore false despite completion. We
retain that observation rather than weakening the comparison or claiming a
floating certificate. The original integer determinant is28 and its Gram
determinant784, but a matching covolume alone would not establish lattice
equality. The actual unimodular operations do.

The figure compares actual full three-dimensional row norms, without projecting
the lattice into a misleading two-dimensional geometry. Original and returned
row positions are labelled as row indices, not claims of one-to-one shortened
vector identities after swaps.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/lll_original.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/lll.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    std::vector<std::vector<long long>> b{{201, 37, 5}, {143, 25, 3},
                                          {88, 16, 2}};
    auto t = dm::algorithms::lll_trace(b);
    auto &a = t.analysis;
    std::vector<double> x, before, after;
    std::print("| row index | original x | original y | original z | actual returned x | actual returned y " "| actual returned z | observed original squared norm | observed returned squared norm |\n| " "---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < 3; ++i) {
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", i,
                   b[i][0], b[i][1], b[i][2], a.basis[i][0], a.basis[i][1],
                   a.basis[i][2], a.initial_squared_norms[i],
                   a.final_squared_norms[i]);
        x.push_back(i);
        before.push_back(a.initial_squared_norms[i]);
        after.push_back(a.final_squared_norms[i]);
    }
    std::print("\nActual completed {}; computed size-reduced {}; computed Lovasz {}; actual outer steps {}; " "size reductions {}; swaps {}; real GS evaluations {}.\n",
               a.stop == dm::algorithms::LLLStop::Completed,
               a.observed_size_reduced, a.observed_lovasz, a.work.outer_steps,
               a.work.size_reductions, a.work.swaps, a.work.gram_schmidt_runs);
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create(), q = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.points(x, before, "original rows", {220, 38, 38}, 6).title(
        "Actual original3D row norm observations").x_label("original row index").y_label("squared Euclidean row norm");
    q.points(x, after, "actual returned rows", {37, 99, 235}, 6).title(
        "Actual returned3D row norm observations").x_label(
        "returned row index, after possible swaps").y_label(
        "squared Euclidean row norm");
    dm::graphics::RLayout::create(2, 1).add(p).add(q).size(900, 800).title(
        "Original skew basis: full-dimensional norm observations").fit_panels().save_svg("build/lll_original.svg");
}
```
