> Exact transformation evidence is stronger than equal volume

The returned U has integer rows and is produced solely by checked integer row
subtraction and swaps, so its exact mathematical determinant is plus or minus1.
Multiplying U by the original basis yields the returned basis; independent
verification later checks this with arbitrary-precision integers for every
actual state. The table and figure below display the actual native U, not a
transform recovered by floating inversion.

For contrast, bases[(2,0),(0,1)] and[(1,0),(0,2)] both have Gram determinant4
but generate different integer sublattices: only the second contains(1,0). Equal
Gram determinant is a necessary volume comparison, not a sufficient same-lattice
certificate. This report uses the actual elementary-operation witness instead.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/lll_transform.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/lll.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto t =
        dm::algorithms::lll_trace({{201, 37, 5}, {143, 25, 3}, {88, 16, 2}});
    auto &u = t.analysis.transform;
    std::print("Actual integer row transform U, with returned basis = U times original basis:\n\n| actual " "returned row | original row0 coefficient | original row1 coefficient | original row2 " "coefficient |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < u.size(); ++i) {
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", i, u[i][0], u[i][1], u[i][2]);
        for (std::size_t j = 0; j < u[i].size(); ++j)
            p.text(j, -double(i), std::to_string(u[i][j]), {31, 41, 55}, 18);
    }
    std::print("\nActual captured states {}; actual event records {}; complete logical capture entries " "{}.\n",
               t.states.size(), t.events.size(), t.captured_entries);
    p.size(850, 700).x_limits(-.5, 2.5).y_limits(-2.5, .5).title(
        "Actual checked integer transform U").x_label("original input basis row index").y_label("negative returned basis row index").save_svg("build/lll_transform.svg");
}
```
