> Explicit budgets and floating breakdown limits

Each budget below is an independent bounded run on the original skew basis, not
a prefix rerun used to reconstruct the trace. StepLimit returns an equivalent
partial integer basis and exact transform, with no “reduced” completion claim.
The ordinary legacy method uses the same producer with a100000-step budget and
throws on exhaustion. Actual action counts, rather than a theoretical polynomial
bound, describe this finite-precision implementation.

A zero computed orthogonal norm throws as numerical breakdown. It can occur on a
truly dependent basis or because converting very large distinct integers to
double loses their difference. For[(LLONG_MAX,1),(LLONG_MAX−1,1)], the exact
determinant is1, yet both large first coordinates round to the same double. This
is not an exact-rank certificate. Rounded multipliers and every exact
basis/transform coordinate are range-checked before an unsafe integer cast or
update.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/lll_budget.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/lll.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <limits>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    std::vector<std::vector<long long>> b{{201, 37, 5}, {143, 25, 3},
                                          {88, 16, 2}};
    std::vector<double> x, y;
    std::print("| explicit independent outer budget | actual outer steps | actual completed | computed " "size-reduced observation | computed Lovasz observation |\n| ---: | ---: | --- | --- | --- " "|\n");
    for (std::size_t budget : {0, 1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 64}) {
        auto a = dm::algorithms::lll_analyze(b, .75, budget);
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", budget, a.work.outer_steps,
                   a.stop == dm::algorithms::LLLStop::Completed,
                   a.observed_size_reduced, a.observed_lovasz);
        x.push_back(budget);
        y.push_back(a.work.outer_steps);
    }
    const auto m = std::numeric_limits<long long>::max();
    bool breakdown = false;
    try {
        auto a = dm::algorithms::lll_analyze({{m, 1}, {m - 1, 1}});
    } catch (const std::domain_error &) {
        breakdown = true;
    }
    std::print("\nActual floating GS breakdown on the explicit exact-determinant1 control: {}.\n",
               breakdown);
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.points(x, y, "actual outer iterations", {37, 99, 235}, 6).title(
        "Actual bounded LLL runs on the original basis").x_label(
        "explicit independent outer-step budget").y_label(
        "actual performed outer steps").save_svg("build/lll_budget.svg");
}
```
