\caption(Actual independent budget outcomes and a full-rank floating-breakdown control.)
\alttext(Budget exhaustion is explicit and every returned partial basis remains equivalent; a computed zero orthogonal norm is not misreported as mathematical rank deficiency.)

> Contracts and verification

Nonempty bases are rectangular with positive coordinate dimension and at most
that many rows; delta is finite in(0.25,1). Actual computed orthogonal norms
must be positive finite. Basis and transform coordinates are signed64 long long,
with exact widened product/subtraction and checked narrowing; no
arbitrary-precision fallback or guaranteed support for every mathematically
reducible full-range basis is implied. Complete ordinary finite decision order
is retained, with shared actual GS state used for observations. Empty input is
valid and produces no GS state.

For n rows and dimension d, each actual captured state counts1+2*n*d+2*n*n+n
logical input/transform/orthogonal/projection/norm records, plus n*d original
coordinates and one record per actual event. States/events are admitted before
their copies; unknown future operations are not fabricated. Default cap is one
million,0 disables only that optional cap, and scalar fields/row
headers/capacities/result/runtime copies/bytes are excluded. Captures own
complete actual states with no prefix reconstruction.

Native tests verify exact unimodular identities in every actual captured state
and across 169 triangular integer families, retain the original skew basis and
tiny reduction, and check explicit budgets, numerical breakdown, integer range
guards, quotas and ownership. The ten-report batch passed 101 native CTest
cases, 34 directly instrumented ASan/UBSan cases, 103 compiled/executed public
examples, 515/515 scoped file definitions plus 10 exact LCG class definitions,
and ten representative clangd hovers. Independent Python integer/Fraction,
explicit-label graph search, quadratic sequence DP and full weighted-stump
references passed 69430 records across all ten topics, including a separately
fitted held-out Iris model. Frozen ordinary compatibility passed 1000 Lex-BFS
orders, 1000 library sorts, 100 LBG codebooks, 100 complete five-round
LogitBoost ensembles and 200 LLL bases; corrected LBG final labels/objectives
are intentionally excluded from historical compatibility. All 4 complete
programs executed and all 4 native figures were rendered and visually reviewed,
with clipped legends corrected and rerun. HTML/Markdown computed-result and
figure-byte checks gate legacy retirement. Repeatable receipts are retained in
`build/mepml-conversion/batch-204-213/`.

> References

A. K. Lenstra, H. W. Lenstra Jr. and L. Lovasz(1982),
[Factoring Polynomials with Rational Coefficients|https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01457454],
Mathematische Annalen261,515–534. The exact-arithmetic row-operation rationale
is retained, while the implementation’s floating decisions, bounded storage and
finite budget are explicit limits on any reduction-quality claim.
